# `remove-restrictions` on the deployed site, and what other people's readers said about the download

Two runs of `scripts/live-remove-restrictions-proof.mjs` against
`https://www.browsersnip.com` (the build deployed from this branch), each driven the
way a person drives it: open the tool, drop the file, read what the file's card says
about the lock, type the open password into the box on that card, press
**Remove restrictions**, press **Download**. Then the downloaded bytes are judged by
libqpdf, MuPDF, pypdf and poppler — never by the card.

The first file is `tests/fixtures/encrypted/aes-256-user.pdf`: written by libqpdf
12.3.2, `/V 5 /R 6 /CFM /AESV3`, user secret `hunter2`, `/P = -3376` (print, edit,
copy, annotate, form-fill and assemble refused). The second is its
**restricted-but-openable** twin `aes-256-owner.pdf`, whose user secret is empty, so
that run types nothing at all — it is the shape the triage row's own words call
"password protected" while five readers call it open.

`has_encrypt_key` / `has_P_key` / `has_CFM_key` are greps of the download for the
trailer entry, the permission dictionary and the crypt filter; `*_opens_with_no_password`
/ `mupdf_needs_pass` are the gate; `mupdf_permissions = -4` is every restriction bit
set; `mupdf_planted_pages` counts the sheets still carrying the planted sentence;
`mupdf_ink_page1_percent` is the non-white share of a 72 dpi raster of sheet 1, which
is the fixture's own 1.51 %; `mupdf_toc_entries` is the two-level outline;
`qpdf_check_exit` is `qpdf --check`; `secret_in_bytes` is the typed password in the
clear.

## the user-password run (`hunter2` typed into the file card)

# https://www.browsersnip.com · remove-restrictions · aes-256-user.pdf · secret "hunter2"
route : #/tool/remove-restrictions
intake: file input present, accept=.pdf,application/pdf
card  : ENCRYPTED WITH AES-256 (CRYPT FILTER /STDCF, REVISION 6) /  / This file needs its password before anything here can read its pages. /  / PASSWORD FOR THIS FILE
typed : typed into aes-256-user.pdf · aria-label="Open password for aes-256-user.pdf"
run   : clicked <button> Remove restrictions
result: Restrictions cleared — 3 page(s) verified readable with no /Encrypt entry and no password needed, carrying 1 bookmark(s).
notes : Page 1 of 3 of aes-256-user_unrestricted.pdf, drawn in this tab — a picture of the file, not the file itself. / aes-256-user_unrestricted.pdf / Restrictions cleared — 3 page(s) verified readable with no /Encrypt entry and no password needed, carrying 1 bookmark(s).
down  : clicked <button> Download
name  : aes-256-user_unrestricted.pdf
file  : /tmp/live-restrictions-r3BPit/deployed-unrestricted.pdf 2816 bytes
errors: []
# outside readers, on the file the deployed site downloaded
